description:
order.updated subscriber → address/contact edit re-sync (status-gated)

Split out from #31 during M2 planning. Research against Medusa 2.16.0 confirmed that `order-edit.confirmed` carries ONLY line-item/shipping `ITEM_*`/`SHIPPING_*` actions; address/billing/email/contact changes go through `updateOrderWorkflow`, which emits **`order.updated`** with payload `{ id }` only (no actions array). The change detail lives on the `update_order` order-change's `details.type` (`shipping_address` | `billing_address` | `email` | `metadata` | `locale`).

Implement a subscriber on `order.updated` that:
- re-queries the order from `{ id }` (the payload carries no actions);
- detects address/contact/email changes (re-query the latest `update_order` order-change `details.type`, or diff the order);
- resolves `OngoingOrderSync` + cached `latest_status_code`, consults `edit_sync_rules.address_contact`;
- allowed → run `syncOrderEditToOngoing` (#27); blocked → skip + warning event;
- never throws; idempotent.

Pairs with #31 (line-items-only on `order-edit.confirmed`). Together they cover spec §8's `edit_sync_rules` categories (`address_contact`, `line_items`).

Spec: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-23-ongoing-warehouse-fulfillment-plugin-design.md (§8, §13.3)
